                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you still remember games like Jagged Alliance or Fallout Tactics, you will probably feel right at home here. The game has A LOT (!) of options to customize and craft your team (...prisoners, weapons and weapon modifications, items, bionics, mutations...you get the point...) and the artwork is absolutely fantastic if you where into 80/90's comics. I also enjoy the cheezy/trashy humor that probably was inspired by everything from TMNT to Terminator and more than just a couple of saturday morning cartoons.\n\nDue to the game's tactical and customization complexity, it took me a while to get into it though but it grew on me. My only negative so far is that the models look the same on the battle maps. It would have been nice to have different models, even though the profile pic serves it's purpose well to tell them appart.\n\nIf you look for a 90's tactics game remade for today and some neon-light cyber nostalgia then go ahead - you can't go wrong with this one.",
